module

public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.GroupAlgGeom.EquationallyNoetherian
public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.GroupAlgGeom.Irreducible.Basic

/-!
# Separated groups are coordinate groups

Let `K` be a group receiving the coefficients `G` through `κ : G →* K` and generated over `G` by
the images of the variables `X`, that is, presented by a surjective `G`-homomorphism
`π : G[X] →* K`. Then `K` is separated by `H` (over `G`) if and only if the kernel of `π` is its
own radical over `H`. In that case `π` identifies the coordinate group `G_{R(S)}` of the system
`S = ker π` with `K`, so the groups separated by `H` and generated by `X` over `G` are exactly the
coordinate groups over `H` in the variables `X`.

One direction needs no surjectivity. If `K` is separated by `H`, the equations vanishing on the
points `ψ ∘ p` of `H^X`, for a tuple `p : X → K` and `ψ` ranging over the homomorphisms `K → H`
over `G`, are exactly those vanishing at `p` in `K`. Hence the kernel of any `G`-homomorphism
`π : G[X] →* K` is its own radical over `H`, and if `K` is discriminated by `H`, the algebraic set
of `ker π` is irreducible, its coordinate group embedding in `K`.

Three special cases are recorded. Every coordinate group `G_{R(S)}` is separated by `H`. The group
`G_S = G[X] ⧸ ncl(S)` of a system is separated by `H` exactly when the radical of `S` is its
normal closure. Over `F(a, b)` the group of the system `x² = 1` is not separated by `F(a, b)`,
because the radical of `x²` is the normal closure of `x`.

Combined with the characterization of irreducible algebraic sets by discrimination, this gives a
recognition theorem for discriminated groups: if `H` is equationally Noetherian and `X` is finite,
then `K` is discriminated by `H` if and only if it is `G`-isomorphic to the coordinate group of an
irreducible algebraic set defined by a finite system. This applies for instance to a free group
of finite rank over itself, which is equationally Noetherian. Over a domain `H`, discrimination is
separation plus being a domain, so a nonempty algebraic set is irreducible exactly when its
coordinate group is a domain over `G`. That a domain coordinate group makes a nonempty algebraic
set irreducible needs no hypothesis on `H`. In particular a nonempty algebraic set with a CSA
coordinate group is irreducible as soon as two coefficients do not commute in `H`, since a CSA
group is a domain over any coefficients that do not commute.

No hypothesis on the coefficient maps is needed: they are arbitrary homomorphisms, so the results
also cover systems without solutions, whose coordinate group is trivial.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.isSeparatedBy_iff_Rad_ker_eq`: a group presented over `G` by `π` is
  separated by `H` if and only if `Rad_H(ker π) = ker π`.
* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.IsSeparatedBy.I_range_comp_eq_ker_eval`: for `K` separated by `H`, the
  equations vanishing on the points `ψ ∘ p` are the kernel of the evaluation at `p`.
* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.IsSeparatedBy.Rad_ker_eq`: for `K` separated by `H`, the kernel of any
  homomorphism `G[X] →* K` over `G` is its own radical.
* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.IsDiscriminatedBy.isIrreducible_V_ker`: for `K` discriminated by `H`, the
  algebraic set of that kernel is irreducible.
* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.CoordGroup.isSeparatedBy_coeff`: coordinate groups over `H` are separated
  by `H`.
* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.SystemGroup.isSeparatedBy_coeff_iff`: `G_S` is separated by `H` if and
  only if `Rad_H(S) = ncl(S)`.
* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.isSeparatedBy_iff_exists_coordGroup`: a group generated over `G` by the
  images of `X` is separated by `H` if and only if it is `G`-isomorphic to a coordinate group over
  `H` in the variables `X`.
* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.isDiscriminatedBy_iff_exists_coordGroup`: over an equationally
  Noetherian `H` and for finite `X`, such a group is discriminated by `H` if and only if it is
  `G`-isomorphic to the coordinate group of an irreducible algebraic set defined by a finite
  system.
* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.isIrreducible_V_iff_isGDomain`: over a domain `H`, a nonempty algebraic
  set is irreducible if and only if its coordinate group is a domain over `G`.
* `TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom.isIrreducible_V_of_isCSA`: a nonempty algebraic set with a CSA coordinate
  group is irreducible, provided two coefficients do not commute in `H`.

## References

* G. Baumslag, A. Myasnikov, V. Remeslennikov, *Algebraic geometry over groups I. Algebraic sets
  and ideal theory*, J. Algebra 219 (1999), Theorem C1, §3.4 (Corollary 8) and §4 (Theorem 5).
* O. Kharlampovich, A. Myasnikov, *Irreducible affine varieties over a free group. I:
  Irreducibility of quadratic equations and Nullstellensatz*, J. Algebra 200 (1998), §1,
  Lemmas 3 and 4.
* O. Kharlampovich, A. Myasnikov, *Implicit function theorem over free groups*, J. Algebra 290
  (2005), §2.6.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom

open Monoid.Coprod Subgroup

variable {G H K X : Type*} [Group G] [Group H] [Group K] {ι : G →* H} {κ : G →* K}

namespace GX

/-- A quotient `G[X] ⧸ N` is separated by `H` over `G` if and only if `N` is its own radical
over `H`. -/
theorem isSeparatedBy_quotientCoeff_iff (N : Subgroup (GX G X)) [N.Normal] :
    IsSeparatedBy (quotientCoeff N) ι ↔ Rad ι (N : Set (GX G X)) = N := by
  rw [isSeparatedBy_def]
  refine ⟨fun h => le_antisymm (fun w hw => ?_) (fun w hw => subset_Rad _ hw), fun h q hq => ?_⟩
  · -- A separating homomorphism restricts to a solution of `N` at which `w` survives.
    by_contra hwN
    obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := h (w : GX G X ⧸ N) ((QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff w).not.2 hwN)
    have he := mem_Rad.1 hw _ (quotientHomEquiv ι N φ).2
    rw [eval_quotientHomEquiv] at he
    exact hφ he
  · -- Conversely an element outside `N` lies outside the radical, so some solution sees it.
    obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := QuotientGroup.mk_surjective q
    have hw : w ∉ Rad ι (N : Set (GX G X)) := by
      rw [h]
      exact fun hw => hq ((QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff w).2 hw)
    simp only [mem_Rad, not_forall] at hw
    obtain ⟨v, hv, hvw⟩ := hw
    exact ⟨quotientEvalGHom v hv, by simpa using hvw⟩

end GX

/-- A group `K` generated over `G` by the images of the variables, through a surjective
`G`-homomorphism `π : G[X] →* K`, is separated by `H` if and only if the kernel of `π` is its own
radical over `H`. -/
theorem isSeparatedBy_iff_Rad_ker_eq (π : GHom (inl : G →* GX G X) κ)
    (hπ : Function.Surjective π) :
    IsSeparatedBy κ ι ↔
      Rad ι ((π : GX G X →* K).ker : Set (GX G X)) = (π : GX G X →* K).ker := by
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψ, -⟩ := GX.exists_bijective_gHom_of_eq_ker π hπ rfl
  rw [← GX.isSeparatedBy_quotientCoeff_iff]
  exact ⟨fun h => h.of_injective ψ hψ.1,
    fun h => h.of_injective (ψ.symmOfBijective hψ) (ψ.symmOfBijective_injective hψ)⟩

/-- If `K` is separated by `H` over `G`, an equation vanishes on the image of a tuple `p` of
elements of `K` under all homomorphisms `K → H` over `G` exactly when it vanishes at `p`. -/
theorem IsSeparatedBy.I_range_comp_eq_ker_eval (h : IsSeparatedBy κ ι) (p : X → K) :
    I ι (Set.range fun ψ : GHom κ ι => ψ ∘ p) = (eval κ p).ker := by
  ext w
  simp only [mem_I, Set.forall_mem_range, ← map_eval, MonoidHom.mem_ker]
  refine ⟨fun hw => by_contra fun hne => ?_, fun hw ψ => by rw [hw, map_one]⟩
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψ⟩ := (isSeparatedBy_def _ _).1 h _ hne
  exact hψ (hw ψ)

/-- If `K` is separated by `H` over `G`, the kernel of a homomorphism `G[X] →* K` over `G`,
surjective or not, is its own radical over `H`. -/
theorem IsSeparatedBy.Rad_ker_eq (h : IsSeparatedBy κ ι) (π : GHom (inl : G →* GX G X) κ) :
    Rad ι ((π : GX G X →* K).ker : Set (GX G X)) = (π : GX G X →* K).ker := by
  -- `ker π` is the set of equations vanishing at the points `ψ ∘ π ∘ vars`.
  rw [← eval_eq_of_comp_inl π.comp_coeff, ← h.I_range_comp_eq_ker_eval, Rad_def, I_V_I]

/-- If `K` is discriminated by `H` over `G`, the algebraic set over `H` of the kernel of a
homomorphism `G[X] →* K` over `G`, surjective or not, is irreducible. -/
theorem IsDiscriminatedBy.isIrreducible_V_ker (h : IsDiscriminatedBy κ ι)
    (π : GHom (inl : G →* GX G X) κ) :
    @IsIrreducible (X → H) (zariskiTopology ι X)
      (V ι ((π : GX G X →* K).ker : Set (GX G X))) := by
  have hRad := h.isSeparatedBy.Rad_ker_eq π
  rw [isIrreducible_V_iff_isDiscriminatedBy, CoordGroup.coeff_def]
  -- The coordinate group of the kernel embeds in `K` over `G`.
  exact h.of_injective ⟨QuotientGroup.lift _ (π : GX G X →* K) hRad.le, fun g => by simp⟩
    ((QuotientGroup.injective_lift_iff _ _ hRad.le).2 hRad)

/-- The coordinate group `G_{R(S)}` is separated by `H`. -/
theorem CoordGroup.isSeparatedBy_coeff (S : Set (GX G X)) :
    IsSeparatedBy (CoordGroup.coeff ι S) ι := by
  rw [CoordGroup.coeff_def, GX.isSeparatedBy_quotientCoeff_iff, Rad_Rad]

/-- The group `G_S = G[X] ⧸ ncl(S)` of a system is separated by `H` if and only if the radical of
`S` over `H` is the normal closure of `S`. -/
theorem SystemGroup.isSeparatedBy_coeff_iff (S : Set (GX G X)) :
    IsSeparatedBy (SystemGroup.coeff S) ι ↔ Rad ι S = normalClosure S := by
  rw [SystemGroup.coeff_def, GX.isSeparatedBy_quotientCoeff_iff, Rad_normalClosure]

/-- Over `F(a, b)` with one variable `x`, the group of the system `x² = 1` is not separated by
`F(a, b)`: the radical of `x²` is the normal closure of `x`, not that of `x²`. -/
theorem SystemGroup.not_isSeparatedBy_coeff_sq :
    ¬IsSeparatedBy
      (SystemGroup.coeff {(inr (FreeGroup.of ()) : GX (FreeGroup (Fin 2)) Unit) ^ 2})
      (.id (FreeGroup (Fin 2))) := by
  rw [SystemGroup.isSeparatedBy_coeff_iff, rad_sq.1]
  exact rad_sq.2.symm

/-- A group `K` generated over `G` by the images of the variables `X` is separated by `H` if and
only if it is `G`-isomorphic to a coordinate group over `H` in the variables `X`. -/
theorem isSeparatedBy_iff_exists_coordGroup (π : GHom (inl : G →* GX G X) κ)
    (hπ : Function.Surjective π) :
    IsSeparatedBy κ ι ↔
      ∃ (S : Set (GX G X)) (φ : GHom (CoordGroup.coeff ι S) κ), Function.Bijective φ := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ⟨(π : GX G X →* K).ker, ?_⟩, fun ⟨S, φ, hφ⟩ =>
    (CoordGroup.isSeparatedBy_coeff S).of_injective (φ.symmOfBijective hφ)
      (φ.symmOfBijective_injective hφ)⟩
  rw [CoordGroup.coeff_def]
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψ, -⟩ := GX.exists_bijective_gHom_of_eq_ker π hπ (h.Rad_ker_eq π)
  exact ⟨ψ, hψ⟩

/-- Over an equationally Noetherian group `H`, a group `K` generated over `G` by the images of
finitely many variables `X` is discriminated by `H` if and only if it is `G`-isomorphic to the
coordinate group of an irreducible algebraic set defined by a finite system. -/
theorem isDiscriminatedBy_iff_exists_coordGroup [Finite X] (hH : IsEquationallyNoetherian ι)
    (π : GHom (inl : G →* GX G X) κ) (hπ : Function.Surjective π) :
    IsDiscriminatedBy κ ι ↔
      ∃ S : Set (GX G X), S.Finite ∧ @IsIrreducible (X → H) (zariskiTopology ι X) (V ι S) ∧
        ∃ φ : GHom (CoordGroup.coeff ι S) κ, Function.Bijective φ := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, fun ⟨S, _, hS, φ, hφ⟩ =>
    (isIrreducible_V_iff_isDiscriminatedBy.1 hS).of_injective (φ.symmOfBijective hφ)
      (φ.symmOfBijective_injective hφ)⟩
  -- The kernel of `π` is its own radical, which a finite subsystem already defines.
  have hker := h.isSeparatedBy.Rad_ker_eq π
  obtain ⟨S, -, hfin, hRad⟩ := hH.exists_finite_Rad_eq ((π : GX G X →* K).ker : Set (GX G X))
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψ, -⟩ := GX.exists_bijective_gHom_of_eq_ker π hπ (hRad.trans hker)
  refine ⟨S, hfin, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [isIrreducible_V_iff_isDiscriminatedBy, CoordGroup.coeff_def]
    exact h.of_injective ψ hψ.1
  · rw [CoordGroup.coeff_def]
    exact ⟨ψ, hψ⟩

/-- A nonempty algebraic set whose coordinate group is a domain over `G` is irreducible. No
hypothesis on `H` is needed. Nonemptiness is needed: the empty set is not irreducible, while its
trivial coordinate group is a domain. -/
theorem isIrreducible_V_of_isGDomain {S : Set (GX G X)} (hS : (V ι S).Nonempty)
    (h : IsGDomain (CoordGroup.coeff ι S)) :
    @IsIrreducible (X → H) (zariskiTopology ι X) (V ι S) := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hS
  rw [isIrreducible_V_iff_isDiscriminatedBy]
  exact (CoordGroup.isSeparatedBy_coeff S).isDiscriminatedBy h ⟨CoordGroup.evalGHom v hv⟩

/-- Over a domain `H` over `G`, a nonempty algebraic set is irreducible if and only if its
coordinate group is a domain over `G`. Nonemptiness is needed: the empty set is not irreducible,
while its trivial coordinate group is a domain. -/
theorem isIrreducible_V_iff_isGDomain {S : Set (GX G X)} (hH : IsGDomain ι)
    (hS : (V ι S).Nonempty) :
    @IsIrreducible (X → H) (zariskiTopology ι X) (V ι S) ↔
      IsGDomain (CoordGroup.coeff ι S) :=
  ⟨fun h => (isIrreducible_V_iff_isDiscriminatedBy.1 h).isGDomain hH,
    isIrreducible_V_of_isGDomain hS⟩

/-- A nonempty algebraic set whose coordinate group is CSA is irreducible, as soon as two
coefficients do not commute in `H`. They then do not commute in the coordinate group either,
which makes the CSA coordinate group a domain over `G`. This applies to fully residually free
coordinate groups over a nonabelian free group. -/
theorem isIrreducible_V_of_isCSA {S : Set (GX G X)} (hS : (V ι S).Nonempty)
    (hCSA : Group.IsCSA (CoordGroup ι S)) {a b : G} (hab : ¬Commute (ι a) (ι b)) :
    @IsIrreducible (X → H) (zariskiTopology ι X) (V ι S) := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hS
  refine isIrreducible_V_of_isGDomain ⟨v, hv⟩ (.of_isCSA hCSA (a := a) (b := b) fun h => hab ?_)
  simpa only [GHom.map_coeff] using h.map (CoordGroup.evalGHom v hv)

end TauCeti.GroupAlgGeom
